<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>G7 talks in Paris try to tackle global crises with uncertainty high over US approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddf2f1410477c48f8a059e0250bc006776357c06b826e5689f6e06a72645c7d4</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:12:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-g7-talks-in-paris-try-to-tackle-global-crises-with-uncertainty-high-over-us-approach--b50e90101c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-g7-talks-in-paris-try-to-tackle-global-crises-with-uncertainty-high-over-us-approach" /><summary type="html">Top diplomats from the Group of Seven industrialized democracies gathered in Paris on Monday with clear differences on global crises and questions about how U.S. President Donald Trump will approach foreign policy after his Republican Party’s heavy losses in the midterm elections. Whether on the Russia-Ukraine war, Iran or the International Criminal Court, the sides appeared far apart as two days of talks got underway, as FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘It’s a farce’: Hegseth slams impeachment effort</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228c62c09ded66f69f3e37d64127ee86699073fdf6ea862f4199385ad8641d09</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:10:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-it-s-a-farce-hegseth-slams-impeachment-effort--cebec3b1997b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-it-s-a-farce-hegseth-slams-impeachment-effort" /><summary type="html">US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth dismissed a move to impeach him by a Republican lawmaker as a “farce” and a political “stunt” on Tuesday. It came a day after outgoing US Representative Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment against Hegseth over his handling of the war with Iran and other alleged abuses of power.</summary></entry><entry><title>The robot boom: Are businesses ready for an AI-powered workforce?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d00c1eba3f146f3befc637b083d5204bfd3507a68b6964875d0c76c8d17ede6</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:01:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261110-the-robot-boom-are-businesses-ready-for-an-ai-powered-workforce--27ebe407cc42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261110-the-robot-boom-are-businesses-ready-for-an-ai-powered-workforce" /><summary type="html">As artificial intelligence makes machines more capable and autonomous, businesses are racing to embrace robotics. But while many executives expect to deploy robot fleets in the coming years, far fewer have a clear strategy for doing so. FRANCE 24's Charles Pellegrin speaks to John Healy, Intel's Vice President of Robotics and Industrial Solutions, about the opportunities, risks and workforce challenges behind the growing robot revolution.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Israel live: Eisenkot party submits bill to new parliament to investigate October 7 failures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:618c8f41710d911dc792989d37d2d890cbe2a34a6ed7fddfee25c2f12348a2e4</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:40:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-live-new-israeli-parliament-sworn-in-eisenkot-aims-to-form-government-netanyahu-knesset" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament was sworn in Tuesday with opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot aiming to build a coalition after receiving a mandate to form a government. Eisenkot's party moved to immediately set up a commission to investigate failures that allowed Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, a move long resisted by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Follow our live coverage for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Clean beauty': How to navigate the latest cosmetic and skincare trends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ff004ba372c472fa1d226d344de7fa9248e13272536768a382d6aa709b6ed08</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:11:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261110-clean-beauty-how-to-navigate-the-latest-cosmetic-and-skincare-trends--778e8d56a286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261110-clean-beauty-how-to-navigate-the-latest-cosmetic-and-skincare-trends" /><summary type="html">It's hard to believe, but Christmas is just six weeks away. That means the battle of the Advent calendars is now well and truly underway. So if you love beauty products but are wanting to buy with safety and a healthy approach in mind, what do you do? Joining us from Atlanta is Lisa Fennessy, the founder and CEO of The New Knew, which reviews "clean beauty" products. She tells us what to look out for to take better care of our skin.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Pokemon's 30-year anniversary: Japanese cards sell like wildfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a353da5336fa5c4e957897ce8cab40863ff1f8e67751c99fc35bef5a86e70616</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-pokemon-s-30-year-anniversary-japanese-cards-sell-like-wildfire--78c6f75eaa94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-pokemon-s-30-year-anniversary-japanese-cards-sell-like-wildfire" /><summary type="html">Pokemon, the famous Japanese little monsters, are turning 30, and their trading cards are selling like wildfire, often being flipped for small fortunes. People prepared to camp outside specialised shops in a bid to buy some of these cards.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pentagon chief Pete Hegseth calls move to impeach him 'sabotage'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0eb6652b190c57cd25338130666dce8f63048b541cb03baec18b103595ca6712</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:32:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-live-pentagon-chief-pete-hegseth-calls-move-to-impeach-him-a-farce" /><summary type="html">US ​Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth on Tuesday called ​moves to impeach him over abuse of power in the Iran war a farce that ​would ‌fail. The Pentagon chief slammed the move as a "political spectacle" by an outgoing congressional opponent of President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US-mediated talks on ending Russia-Ukraine war begin in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67aabd9cc0cc88c6340073cb22f88bbb48528903e5099ef3711e464f2cdd56f1</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Three-way talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US opened Tuesday, November 10, in the United Arab Emirates, as Washington made another push to end the war. The two-day session in Abu Dhabi is the first such meeting since February. It will focus on establishing future security guarantees for the warring countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students block dozens of schools, vow more protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a648e0da2e39492b27c711ba961c8d39611957b1ef14eb382a097cbe7f797ef</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests" /><summary type="html">French students blocked the entrances to dozens of high schools on Tuesday, November 10, as they kept up protests for better learning conditions. These protests across France have spiraled into larger cost-of-living demonstrations in recent weeks, some marked by violence and police brutality. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine peace talks: Who is sitting at the negotiating table – and why it matters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:471259abae9fc216977fa54c9d36fcc105958c608a4b06c936eb0ddd3eab52da</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:45:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-ukraine-peace-talks-who-is-sitting-at-the-negotiating-table-_-and-why-it-matters--68903cc62b2a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-ukraine-peace-talks-who-is-sitting-at-the-negotiating-table-%E2%80%93-and-why-it-matters" /><summary type="html">Three-way talks between Russia, Ukraine and the United States opened Tuesday in the United Arab Emirates, as Washington made a renewed push to end the war that followed Moscow's invasion of its neighbour nearly five years ago. As these two days of talks in Abu Dhabi get underway, the negotiators that each country has chosen to send tell us most of what we need to know about what will be discussed, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dana White: UFC chief declines Trump’s White House job offer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43cfe4d47c154c90acff0867a7336dc6d1e2aeb05c3310c0961e43ee766cc976</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:39:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-dana-white-ufc-chief-declines-trump-s-white-house-job-offer--f2546479adb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-dana-white-ufc-chief-declines-trump-s-white-house-job-offer" /><summary type="html">Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) chief Dana White made a surprise appearance at the White House on Monday to turn down Donald Trump’s offer of a job as the White House press secretary, saying he has “zero political aspirations”. Trump stunned the world on November 7 when he said on social media that he had offered White the job, only to claim a day later that he was "only kidding”.</summary></entry><entry><title>New Israel parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot works to form new govt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fa77553ee1490ec32781e98508d91f3ef5732adc3ff66baf9d1f2971a72bee2</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt--82de353b7556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament will be sworn on Tuesday, November 10, with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu set to lose his majority as rival Gadi Eisenkot works to form a new government. The opposition hopes to use its newfound legislative power to move quickly on key priorities, including a commission to investigate security failures under Netanyahu that allowed the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>California voters reject measure to tax the wealth of billionaires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:877584fdb9da1bb5d73fb86fe8fcf6c82a7ab6658bd391c1f0e8c59a1da87d00</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:20:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-california-voters-reject-measure-to-tax-the-wealth-of-billionaires--c30b5a0e4d33.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-california-voters-reject-measure-to-tax-the-wealth-of-billionaires" /><summary type="html">California voters have rejected a first-in-the-nation tax on the net worth of billionaires following a contentious ballot fight that generated huge spending by some prominent tech leaders eager to stop their taxes from going up. The measure would have imposed a one-time 5% tax on the wealth of Californians whose net worth exceeds $1 billion. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Los Angeles Loic Pialat has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Teddy Riner: From French Olympic judo champion to presidential candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25703395973a9773baa6640311a86ddd170b067b3bac1ef317b27807f99cfda6</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:16:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261110-teddy-riner-from-french-olympic-judo-champion-to-presidential-candidate--4ea0b0e8b97d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261110-teddy-riner-from-french-olympic-judo-champion-to-presidential-candidate" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, November 10: French Olympic judo champion Teddy Riner announces he will run for president in next year's French elections. But how serious is his bid? Also, a new government directive in France says schoolchildren must participate in Remembrance Day commemorations – but the unions are not happy. British comedian Russell Brand is sentenced to 10 years in prison for rape and sexual assault. Finally, we bring you the best of the memes on Nvidia's Jensen Huang.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>US Hegseth faces Republican impeachment bid over abuse of power in Iran war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2f725100a367fc2927078819bf37ebdaa85ea392bcddcc03f32c49f120bf9e6</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:03:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-hegseth-faces-republican-impeachment-bid-over-abuse-of-power-in-iran-war--d654a3d11c99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-hegseth-faces-republican-impeachment-bid-over-abuse-of-power-in-iran-war" /><summary type="html">A Republican lawmaker moved on Monday to impeach US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth over the war in Iran, setting the stage for a potentially explosive vote in Congress, days after President Donald Trump's party suffered a crushing defeat in the midterms. Kentucky Congressman Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment, accusing Hegseth of waging war illegally without congressional authorisation and abusing his powers as Pentagon chief.</summary></entry><entry><title>China's charm offensive pays off as foreign tourism rebounds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fbc888115404e3d46f690f109cb637854f54c9f9eb276ac04b14c82637febd9</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:58:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-china-s-charm-offensive-pays-off-as-foreign-tourism-rebounds--77b825a4122e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-china-s-charm-offensive-pays-off-as-foreign-tourism-rebounds" /><summary type="html">How is tourism faring in China seven years after the Covid-19 pandemic? The country reopened its borders in 2023 and is playing the charm card to restore its image. A strategy that’s paying off: last year the number of tourists exceeded pre-pandemic levels, and French travelers are among those flocking there.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguayan protesters are back on the streets despite the removal of President</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44d37dad0f0ad606d15fc5ff75d59aa097c3248e168946937719a57b99403616</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:53:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-paraguayan-protesters-are-back-on-the-streets-despite-the-removal-of-president--9d1f87be900c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-paraguayan-protesters-are-back-on-the-streets-despite-the-removal-of-president" /><summary type="html">A banking crisis that saw the president of Paraguay impeached Friday, November 6, continues to rock the country with protesters back on the streets. The Ueno Bank started as a digital first bank, attracting many low income customers, quickly growing to become a major bank in charge of state pensions and holding the accounts of several government institutions before having its accounts frozen by the central bank due to solvency concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>France vows tough response to freezer cyberattack blamed on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f3f49e1b2538c453179413ec4ad6c681d752c1bca465ce4f1d4f0e3f7df3243</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:51:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran--fb059c4de0f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran" /><summary type="html">France's Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot said Tuesday, November 10, that Paris ruled out "nothing" to respond to a major cyberattack on hundreds of supermarket fridges in October that it has blamed on Iran. The goal, Jean-Noel Barrot told France Info, is "to deter anyone who might be tempted, in Iran or elsewhere, to do it again".</summary></entry><entry><title>Seniors rock the stage: Greek theater seeks to show that 'art has no age'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d710bd3b56f27b6f24a19a998b904662ddd465f62cfbc1416645870890121a1b</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:50:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age--d63b9739c4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age" /><summary type="html">A recent Greek National Opera production afforded a group of seniors the chance to channel their young-at-heart energy into onstage performances, proving that no one's too old to learn something new. It challenged the premise that retirement means surrendering to a sedentary lifestyle and extinguishing one’s creative spirit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Peru gets ready to welcome Pope Leo XIV on his South America tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95f8936314a7da963a9dd7056b2abcabe2bbc5b3ae50ff8e8ac188ce75a3143</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-peru-gets-ready-to-welcome-pope-leo-xiv-on-his-south-america-tour--8a71beaecfda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-peru-gets-ready-to-welcome-pope-leo-xiv-on-his-south-america-tour" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV continued his South American tour on Wednesday, November 11, with a visit to Peru, after stops in Uruguay and Argentina. The American-born pontiff lived in Peru for several years and even became a Peruvian citizen. Ahead of his arrival, the country unveiled a giant statue in his honour.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Republican Thomas Massie launches bid to impeach Pete Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb01f3a4d39d6ee208f7f484519b776344e150ef635bd695812e62e91d11408</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:42:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-republican-thomas-massie-launches-bid-to-impeach-pete-hegseth--b093e97a7254.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-republican-thomas-massie-launches-bid-to-impeach-pete-hegseth" /><summary type="html">US Republican Thomas Massie moved Monday, November 9, to force a vote to impeach Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, pressing his fellow Republicans to remove one of the Trump administration's most prominent figures following sweeping election losses blamed in part on fallout from the war in Iran. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine hold US-backed talks after Trump says broad deal is possible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e90c8a1556a11eea059f5196118b9a7b55fc685e57b866ff0e4579da0b365968</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:40:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible--727bc2af7a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible" /><summary type="html">Russian and Ukrainian officials met on Tuesday, November 10, for their first US-brokered talks since February, after US President Donald Trump suggested last week that a broad deal was possible on ending the war in Ukraine and guaranteeing security in Europe. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>China's 'impossible to ignore' tech rise on display at Web Summit in Lisbon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e71d89dccc9d0aea06c6840d0a8d588fb66f4d9b53fbd2d8a1b24a6cb1656e9b</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:22:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261110-china-s-impossible-to-ignore-tech-rise-on-display-at-web-summit-in-lisbon--c646bcff6f60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261110-china-s-impossible-to-ignore-tech-rise-on-display-at-web-summit-in-lisbon" /><summary type="html">One of Europe's biggest annual tech events, the Web Summit, kicked off in the Portuguese capital this week with the biggest ever delegation of Chinese business leaders and policymakers. FRANCE 24's Charles Pellegrin talks to Dr. Dan Wang, China Director at Eurasia Group, about EU-China tech relations, the climate of suspicion created by the spying scandal at Nvidia, and what the EU's quest for tech sovereignty could mean for China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Inspiring Senegal's next generation: Free tickets bring children to Dakar 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab5719b08213365a540103a1c8304c5b0a3ee4a3bbb20e9bb2612f63de8681ed</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:17:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-inspiring-senegal-s-next-generation-free-tickets-bring-children-to-dakar-2026--b4b1089d9ef8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-inspiring-senegal-s-next-generation-free-tickets-bring-children-to-dakar-2026" /><summary type="html">As part of the Dakar 2026 Youth Olympic Games, 200,000 free tickets will be distributed to schools and community organisations. The aim is to give as many young people as possible the chance to experience the Games. FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.</summary></entry></feed>
